<div class="about-description-content">
<p>
You've come to the right place. The Surety Support Forum is where you go to get help with your Surety system. But it's much more than that! It's also the best place on the internet get information on Alarm.com, Qolsys, 2GIG, and other connected home and smart security systems. It's a place to learn, share, or just hang out. You're welcome here, whether or not you're a Surety customer.
</p>

<h2><a href="#surety-customers">Surety Customers</a></h2>
<p>
The support site helps us provide you with the absolute best technical support and customer service in the industry. The forum is staffed by professionals and experts who are prompt, accurate, responsive and understanding. We're here to help you every step of the way.
</p>

<p>
Surety customers enjoy benefits that aren't available to others such as our industry leading self-service tools (<a href="/t/surety-system-manager/30073">System Manager</a>) and the ability for Surety staff to remotely troubleshoot your problems. As a Surety customer you'll have the best Alarm.com experience possible. That's our commitment to you.
</p>

<p>
Don't want to post on a public forum? No problem. You can always <a href="/t/introducing-dexter-the-surety-chatbot/30394">chat with Dexter</a>, <a href="/new-message?groupname=surety">private message</a> or <a href="mailto:support@suretyhome.com">email</a> us. You'll get exceptional quality support whether you interact one on one or participate in the community.
</p>

<h2><a href="#adc-users">Alarm.com Users</a></h2>
<p>
You don't have to be a Surety customer to get help here. If you have an Alarm.com system through another company, you're still welcome. While you won't have access to private support, our self-service tools, and we can't remotely troubleshoot your system for you, we're happy to help any way we can on the public forum.
</p>

<p>
Need help? <a href="/new-topic?category=support">Ask a question</a>. You just might find the Surety community to be your most valuable resource. And you're always welcome to <a href="/t/introducing-dexter-the-surety-chatbot/30394">chat with Dexter</a>.
</p>

<h2><a href="#planning">Planning and Researching</a></h2>
<p>
Not sure which connected home system you want or where to get it? Need help planning and designing your system? No sweat. We have you covered. At Surety we love this stuff so we're happy to answer questions and offer suggestions. We thrive on helping you find creative solutions to your design problems.
</p>

<h2><a href="#enthusiasts">Connected Home &amp; Smart Security Enthusiasts</a></h2>
<p>
It's called the Surety Support Forum but it's bigger than just support. Are you interested in connected homes, home automation and smart security? We want to hear from you. Ask questions. Answer questions. Share your ideas. <a href="/new-topic?category=chat">Let's chat</a>.
</p>

<h2><a href="business-hours">Hours &amp; Availability</a></h2>
<p>
The forum, including <a href="/t/introducing-dexter-the-surety-chatbot/30394">Dexter</a>, is always available to the community, 24/7. Use it any time you like. Our professional monitoring service is active 24/7 as well so we're always there to handle your emergencies.
</p>

<p>
Surety support staff hours are 8:30am - 7:00pm ET Monday - Friday and 10:00am - 2:00pm ET Saturday &amp; Sunday. We are closed on national holidays. We may jump on the forum and answer questions outside of business hours but our commitment to providing prompt and responsive technical support only applies during regular business hours.
</p>
</div>
